WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.100
Our last video explained the famous

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.380
Monty Hall problem. And from what I can

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.390
tell, reading your comments, there are

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:08.580
three types of people here: those who

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.950
understand the problem or even better

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:14.309
were helped by our video, those who still

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:16.740
just don't get it, and those who are

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.050
absolutely adamant that we got it wrong.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.570
But one thing everyone has in common it

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:24.060
seems is a desire to discuss and explain

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.910
how they see the problem. I'm no

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:29.010
different, so what I'd like to do now is

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.840
quickly recap what the Monty Hall

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.690
problem is and then explain to you how I
see it.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:36.390
So we have these three doors: one hides

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.940
this shiny red sports car, the other two

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:41.879
have these worthless goats. You the

00:00:41.879 --> 00:00:44.010
contestant choose a door, let's choose

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.360
door 1 in this example. The gameshow host,

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.379
Monty Hall himself, who knows what's

00:00:49.379 --> 00:00:52.199
behind each door is then forced to

00:00:52.199 --> 00:00:55.110
reveal a goat from behind one of the two

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:57.809
remaining doors. You're then given a

00:00:57.809 --> 00:01:00.989
choice to stick or switch. With two doors

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:02.789
remaining it seems some of you think

00:01:02.789 --> 00:01:05.760
this has become a 50/50 choice, stick or

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.470
switch, it doesn't really matter there

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:09.990
are two doors. One's got the car and one

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:12.600
doesn't; but that's not true and your

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:16.650
best chance of winning is to switch. Now

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.960
the reason for this is an important fact

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.380
that I cannot emphasise enough; Monty

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.470
Hall, the host, knows what's behind all

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:28.470
the doors and he's forced to show you a

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:30.869
goat from behind one of those two

00:01:30.869 --> 00:01:33.200
remaining doors after your first choice.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.150
This is very important. There is

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.280
information here that's about to be put

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.130
into the system, let me explain what

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:43.320
happens. When you made that first choice

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:46.950
there was a 1 in 3 chance that the car

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.619
was behind your door, surely we agree

00:01:49.619 --> 00:01:53.100
here. Now in that situation Monty had two

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:56.189
goats he could have revealed to you from

00:01:56.189 --> 00:01:57.840
behind these other two doors. Now that's

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.270
not very helpful, and of course if you

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.250
then switched like I tell you you should

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:04.649
you'd have moved away from the car and

00:02:04.649 --> 00:02:08.789
lost. I'm sorry, I just lost you a sports

00:02:08.789 --> 00:02:13.280
car, I apologise. But let's be honest,

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:15.590
there was only a 1 in 3 chance of

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:18.110
that happening. Let's wipe the slate

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:20.840
clean, or the brown paper clean, and now

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.180
this time let's imagine your first

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:26.930
choice was that dreaded goat. Now this is

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:29.150
twice as likely, there's a 2 in 3

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.370
chance that this is what you've done. We

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.110
agree on that right? 2 in 3 chance

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:35.300
you've chosen a goat. So this scenario of

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.310
course should be of more interest to us,

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:39.860
it's the more likely scenario. And this

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:43.670
time you have forced Monty's hand. He

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:46.310
knows where the one remaining goat is - he

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:50.330
knows it! And he has to show it to you. In

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:53.690
this case in two thirds of the games you

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:57.200
ever play he is indirectly telling you

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:00.739
exactly where the car is - it's here!

00:03:00.739 --> 00:03:03.950
Behind the door he didn't open! Let me

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.290
say that again, in two thirds of the

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:09.590
games Monty can only open one door

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:12.650
because he knows, and therefore you

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:15.080
should know, the car is behind the other

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:18.339
one. And because you know this you should
switch!

00:03:19.869 --> 00:03:21.590
Now you don't know for sure this

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:23.299
has happened, there's a 1 in 3

00:03:23.299 --> 00:03:25.610
chance this hasn't happened; but there's

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:28.130
a 2 in 3 chance it has happened,

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:30.170
it's more likely to have happened, it's

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:33.340
more probable. So there you go: switch!

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:36.950
Switch! Probability tells you to switch.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.590
And this is because of Monty's knowledge;

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:42.380
if Monty didn't know what was behind the

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:43.489
doors this would be completely

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:45.890
different. Then after his big reveal

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:48.049
you'd be none the wiser and the odds

00:03:48.049 --> 00:03:50.299
would indeed be 50-50, you may as

00:03:50.299 --> 00:03:52.790
well stick. But it's also worth noting in

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.890
that case a third of the time Monty

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:56.780
would accidentally open a door that

00:03:56.780 --> 00:04:00.140
reveals a car! That's not the game we're
playing.

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:02.840
Monty knows where everything is and

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.989
won't reveal the car, that's the rules.

00:04:04.989 --> 00:04:07.010
Monty has the knowledge and therefore

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:09.140
you have the knowledge; and knowledge, as

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:13.350
they say, is power. Leave a comment.

